{
  "requirement": "{cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.criteria.criterion_trait`\n\n`Criterion::source_node_id` identifies the criterion's\n{term}`requirements.sdk.graph.criteria.source_node`:\n\n```rust,ignore\npub trait Criterion<D: Domain>: Send + Sized {\n    // ...\n\n    /// The node this question is about.\n    fn source_node_id(&self) -> NodeId<D>;\n\n    // ...\n}\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The subject's only obligation is that `Criterion::source_node_id` returns the `NodeId<D>` of the criterion's source node, meaning the node the criterion is evaluated on. The cited parent requirement `criterion_trait` only fixes the trait shape, and that shape is exercised by the test's impl.\n\nThe marked test is `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/contracts.rs#fn[criteria_keep_typed_answers_and_persist_only_when_requested]`. It uses the test criterion `Review`, whose `impl[Review<O>/Criterion<Application>]/fn[source_node_id]` returns the stored `source` node.\n\nThe test checks the following:\n- **Source node after verification.** After `validator.verify(descriptor())`, it asserts `value.source_node_id() == &domain.cache().intern_node(Node(1))`. The record's source node therefore has to come from the criterion's `source_node_id`, and any other node would fail.\n- **Source node after storage round-trip.** After `store_evidence` and `load_evidence`, it asserts `loaded.source_node_id() == value.source_node_id()`. The source node survives persistence.\n- **Further coverage.** The `Review` criteria in the same test (the `structure` and `text` paths) also go through `verify` and persist. A second test, `refresh_reuses_current_positive_negative_and_legacy_answers_without_saving`, compares `source_node_id` between reused and saved records. A storage test calls a criterion's `source_node_id` directly.\n\nI found no obligation in the subject that goes untested. The tests only use a single source node, but the text states no behavior that depends on which node it is. The assertion would catch a validator that ignored or replaced the criterion's source node. I found no gap and no acknowledgments apply.",
  "references": "8300e69d2cd42bcc7d0bcdeacb8fd2138a4b03f0b562abfb62cf8af02161f573",
